  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Firms and clients pay for clear drawings, sound judgment and reliability. They judge you by the portfolio, site discipline and communication.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is making a clean, correct drawing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and career options after B.Arch: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools generate images and drafts. Routine visualisation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Design judgment, site understanding and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explore ideas and check them; later, own the design decisions.
  </p>

